@startuml c2-activity
' DOC-9. C2, availability: when a step reads the output of another, does that output exist?
' Card: docs/algorithms/C2.md#pseudocode
' code: flowstat.analysis.availability:analyse
' code: flowstat.analysis.availability:compute
' code: flowstat.analysis.availability:available_at
' code: flowstat.analysis.runs:run_conditions
' code: flowstat.analysis.variables:lower_guards
' code: flowstat.solver.solve:entails
skinparam shadowing false

start
:lower_guards: the guard of every step as a predicate\nand the domain of every variable;
:compute, in plan order;
partition "for every step Y" {
  :runs[Y] = guard(Y) and gate(join(Y), runs of the needs);
  :facts of Y by the rule of its join\n(all_success: OR, any_success and at_least: AND, all_done: nothing);
  :facts of a clean ancestor X |= lo(runs[X])\n(no continue at or above X);
  :drop facts of more than 300 nodes;
}
:analyse: for every reference to X in Y;
if (entails(guard(Y), Av[Y][X]) is UNSAT?) then (the guard proves X ran)
  :the read is safe: no warning;
else (a case is found, or unknown)
  :a warning with the condition and\na value of the inputs that breaks it;
endif
:groups, goals, dead steps, undo: notes and warnings;
stop
@enduml
